{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470198-what-is-the-bare-minimum-of-the-body-needed-to-survive-for-a-vampire","id":1470198,"title":"What is the bare minimum of the body needed to survive for a vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-11T02:36:15-08:00","id":1470198,"title":"What is the bare minimum of the body needed to survive for a vampire?","content":"Let's say an independent ghoul with Vicissitude and surgical skills wants to create his personal Vitae-machine ( drop in pig blood - take out vampiric Vitae ).<br /> <br /> I read that the heart is the main Vitae repository, so a pratical extraction method would be a syringe stuch in the heart, like a tap.<br /> Also, I think the vampire needs at least a stomach to digest the blood into Vitae and a circulatory tract to connect stomach and hearth.<br /> Finally, since vampires are killed by decapitation, you still need to keep the brain.<br /> <br /> So, what can we safely remove ( little by little, to not risk accumulating too much damage )?<br /> <br /> - the limbs, of course<br /> - all internal organs except stomach and heart, so liver, kidneys, lungs, spleen, most of intestine<br /> - all the muscolar apparatus, including tendons and cartilage<br /> - all the skeletal apparatus except mabye the upper part of the spine<br /> - eyes, tongue, jaw, most of the skull<br /> <br /> Mabye also part of the brain, like an extensive lobothomy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T03:07:43-08:00","id":1470203,"title":"","content":"You'd definitely need Visscisitude since otherwise the vampire could regenerate those missing limbs and body parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T04:14:39-08:00","id":1470211,"title":"","content":"If it's a Ghoul, then it would need to be consuming at least 7th gen blood to be able to learn and use Vis 2, which any actual vampire would be able to heal as Agg.<br /> <br /> Assuming it does, first step (after sticking a stake firmly into the heart, even a lomotomite can frenzy...) would be to lobotomize the vamp. (Even without enough Vis, a red hot orbitoclast should be able to pull this off) Once it's brain is non-functional, you're pretty much golden.<br /> <br /> However... Blood needs to go in through the mouth, so that needs to stay. Basically leaving the head and neck and enough of the chest to house the heart is what you're looking at. Once you've got that you could start &quot;shaving off&quot; more, but bare in mind that dealing too much damage may well kill the subject even with non agg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T02:04:04-08:00","id":1470268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470198-what-is-the-bare-minimum-of-the-body-needed-to-survive-for-a-vampire?p=1470203#post1470203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd definitely need Visscisitude since otherwise the vampire could regenerate those missing limbs and body parts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You need at least Vis 2 to work on others anyway (for V20, V5 is different).<br /> <br /> Even without Vicissitude I think it would be reasonable to allow amputation via 'surgical' means to be relatively permanent provided some sort of 'aggravated damage' method was used to close the wounds and the victim remains unconscious or otherwise incapable of acting.<br /> <br /> If you want to see an example of what this would look like watch the Overlord movie - thoroughly recommended<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt4530422/\" target=\"_blank\">Overlord (2018) - IMDb</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T07:56:18-08:00","id":1470279,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of an idea I had for a vampire punishment several years back: every part of the vampire except the head, the heart, and a thin strip of meat connecting the two is chopped away and the vampire is put in a jar. A punishment that pushes the immortality of the vampire right to its limit without crossing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T00:55:45-08:00","id":1470331,"title":"","content":"If you're a powerful Tlacique sorcerer, you can even do away with the strip connecting the two, though the heart would have to remain intact somewhere in order to preserve the decapitated head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T16:07:05-08:00","id":1470383,"title":"","content":"Vampires are undead abominations, they don't follow any biological rules. The old editions even say in the core at some point that the blood actually travels through osmosis rather than by circulation on them.<br /> <br /> So each and every organ must be thought only in terms of symbolic connection. For example, the head is important, but the brain isn't. What exactly about the head is important isn't a thing, s the <i>notion</i> of a head that matters. The other thing is the heart. I think that's it, so I'd go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a>'s punishment idea.<br /> <br /> But bear in mind that this is as valid to a vampire's consciousness and control over the blood as it is to its immortality. It doesn't matter if you lobotomize the undead, their brains are already dead tissue anyway, why would it hold any consciousness in the first place? If the vampire is alive, then it is either torpid or awake and aware. And if it is aware, it has access to the powers of the blood. Without careful maintenance of the &quot;blood processing box&quot; this Ghoul is in for a nasty surprise sooner or later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T16:44:25-08:00","id":1470388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470198-what-is-the-bare-minimum-of-the-body-needed-to-survive-for-a-vampire?p=1470383#post1470383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are undead abominations, they don't follow any biological rules. The old editions even say in the core at some point that the blood actually travels through osmosis rather than by circulation on them.<br /> <br /> So each and every organ must be thought only in terms of symbolic connection. For example, the head is important, but the brain isn't. What exactly about the head is important isn't a thing, s the <i>notion</i> of a head that matters. The other thing is the heart. I think that's it, so I'd go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a>'s punishment idea.<br /> <br /> But bear in mind that this is as valid to a vampire's consciousness and control over the blood as it is to its immortality. It doesn't matter if you lobotomize the undead, their brains are already dead tissue anyway, why would it hold any consciousness in the first place? If the vampire is alive, then it is either torpid or awake and aware. And if it is aware, it has access to the powers of the blood. Without careful maintenance of the &quot;blood processing box&quot; this Ghoul is in for a nasty surprise sooner or later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember naming this punishment the Hom-Dai after the punishment in &quot;The Mummy&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T23:58:28-08:00","id":1470412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/146910-should-personal-peripheral-pools-be-solely-based-off-permanent-essence?p=147038#post147038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It doesn't matter if you lobotomize the undead, their brains are already dead tissue anyway, why would it hold any consciousness in the first place? If the vampire is alive, then it is either torpid or awake and aware. And if it is aware, it has access to the powers of the blood. Without careful maintenance of the &amp;quot;blood processing box&amp;quot; this Ghoul is in for a nasty surprise sooner or later.</div> </div> </div> </div>And with the older vampires, even being torpid isn\u2019t a guarantee they are not aware and even able to use some of their disciplines. VtM is full of examples where torpid Methuselahs continue to use Auspex, Dominate, Presense and the like to maintain their webs of control.<br /> <br /> Dead brain and heart in a jar might be the secret master of an entire empire; particularly since it\u2019s still being fed blood on the regular by the ghoul (who, barring the unbondable merit, is stil blood bound and obsessed with its domitor and might even be doing his master\u2019s will by making it appear that their domitor is off the board when in fact the 6th Gen beast with Auspex 7, Dominate 6 is astrally projecting and dominating the entire Gen 8+ leadership of the city to do its bidding).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}